			],
			"Message": "docs(Common): Refactor README structure and remove decorative elements\n\nRewrite the Common README to improve readability and adhere to project styling guidelines by removing all decorative emojis from headings and non-breaking space artifacts. Compress verbose bullet-point lists into cohesive narrative paragraphs describing the `ActionEffect` system, dependency injection, and transport layers.\n\nUpdate the project structure tree to include new modules (`Telemetry`, `Transport`) and correct formatting for `Configuration`, `IPC`, and `FileSystem` subdirectories. Ensure all links and cross-references remain valid.\n\nThe documentation now focuses on clarity and architectural fidelity without visual clutter.",
			"SHA": "771035143f777fd5a429159d784016b9ee0e835d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T21:14:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠁⠀⠀",
				26,
				11
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize all core submodules with formatting, license, and critical runtime fixes\n\nUpdate 11 core submodules to align with project style standards, correct documentation URLs, and resolve WebKit rendering deadlocks.\n\n**Mountain** adds default configuration options to `Info.plist` and reformats import blocks and provider modules for consistent line-wrapping. **Output** normalizes formatting across the build tree and extends the `PatchWebviewIframeServiceWorker` to enforce `readyState` polling over pathname checks, resolving WebKit bug #238901 that caused Tauri hangs. **Cocoon** and **Wind** reformat ESBuild configurations and regenerate service bridge shapes, while **Rest**, **Worker**, and **SideCar** apply strict code style corrections (quotes, indentation, trailing newlines).\n\n**Grove**, **Mist**, **Vine**, and **Sky** correct license and repository references in their READMEs to point to their respective submodule paths instead of the root `Land` repository.\n\nThese changes ensure build artifact consistency, prevent webview initialization deadlocks, and fix broken documentation links across the element ecosystem.",
			"SHA": "05a609d65c9da8af743e8e95d35f5d0407fb9f5c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T17:50:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Element): Synchronize core submodules with telemetry policy and build fixes\n\nUpdate 6 core submodules to enforce privacy-by-default telemetry policies, resolve native keyring initialization bugs, and standardize build artifacts.\n\n**Common**, **Mountain**, and **Sky** implement a unified telemetry strategy: `Report`, `Capture`, and `OTLPEnabled` defaults are shifted to `false` in `Common` and **Sky**, while **Mountain** defaults remain `true` for development cycle diagnostics but enforce strict runtime consent gates in the `bootstrap-fork.js` sidecar. This ensures data collection only occurs with explicit user or build configuration opt-in.\n\n**Mountain** fixes a critical startup blocker by explicitly initializing the native keyring store (`keyring::use_native_store`) in the binary entry point, resolving 'No default store has been set' errors for extensions like Roo Code. **Maintain** injects runtime environment variables into the `Info.plist` via a new `PlistEdit` module, enabling dev control flags during LaunchServices execution without wrapper scripts. **Output** patches a WebKit Tauri deadlock by enforcing polling-based `DOMContentLoaded` fallbacks and standardizes `Terminal/GPU` directory casing.\n\n**Cocoon** rebuilds artifacts to reflect updated route manifests and casing conventions. These changes stabilize the native backend lifecycle, secure the telemetry pipeline, and resolve platform-specific webview hangs.",
			"SHA": "ac14a2e4555d7b8479ecfafcac1b43d1dad48444"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T16:17:27Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⣿⠃⠀⠀",
				26,
				12
			],
			"Message": "chore(Element): Synchronize all core submodules with fixes and dependency updates\n\nUpdate 11 core submodules across the Land editor stack to incorporate bug fixes, build pipeline corrections, and dependency upgrades.\n\n**Mountain** resolves 4 compile errors in `CreateEffectForRequest`, enhances error handling for keyring access in `SecretProvider`, and standardizes documentation formatting across all provider modules. **Cocoon** and **Wind** normalize gRPC directory casing and type values from \"GRPC\" to \"gRPC\" to align with architectural naming standards, while regenerating interface definitions to match upstream VS Code changes. **Air** corrects gRPC capitalization in validator comments. **Rest** reformats the CLI wrapper script to use single quotes and consistent indentation. **SideCar** updates Node.js versions for target platforms. **Echo**, **Output**, **Wind**, **Worker**, and **Sky** integrate multiple security and feature patches from pnpm, Vitest, Vite, Astro, xterm, and OpenTelemetry ecosystems.\n\nThese updates resolve build failures, ensure strict type safety across the gRPC IPC boundary, and bring all component layers up to date with the latest upstream contributions.",
			"SHA": "9f05dcc5fc3bb67f6e036cdece6deb021b4915a2"
		},
